    <string name="guide_title">Back up games you own</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">Odyssemu plays copies of games you already own. Here is how to make your own backup files. Odyssemu never downloads games for you.</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_title">1. Use your own console and discs</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_body">Only back up discs you bought. Sharing or downloading copies of games you don\'t own is illegal in most countries.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_title">2. Create an image file</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_body">Use your console\'s homebrew tools to dump the disc to an ISO file. CSO is a compressed ISO and works too.</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_title">3. Copy it to your phone</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_body">Connect your phone to a computer and copy the ISO, CSO or PBP files into one folder, for example Games.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_title">4. Pick the folder in Odyssemu</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_body">Open Library › Add games › Choose folder. Odyssemu finds the games and adds covers automatically.</string>

